course: dictionary
lesson: 12152
title: Compensation: making up for a loss
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Compensation is something given to make up for a loss, injury or damage. If your new toy breaks in the shop, the shop may give you a new one as compensation. Look for clues like "loss", "damage" or "injury" to help you spot the meaning.
explain: Read this sentence: «The airline paid us compensation for our late flight.» The flight was late, so the airline gave money to make up for the wait. Compensation is what you get back when something has gone wrong.
explain: Compensation can also be a small good thing that makes a bad thing feel a little better. «The rain spoiled our picnic, but the hot chocolate was some compensation.» The picnic was ruined, so the hot chocolate did not fix everything, but it helped. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Compensation means money or something else given to make up for loss, injury or damage.
fact: «The shop gave her a voucher as compensation for the broken toy.»
fact: Compensation can also mean something that makes a bad thing feel a little better.
fact: In a job, compensation means the pay and benefits you get, such as wages and holidays. This is a more formal use.
fact: Useful phrases: pay compensation, in compensation, as compensation.
exercise: «The airline paid us compensation for our late flight.» What does compensation mean here? | A long wait at the airport | *Money given to make up for the late flight | Sweets for the journey | A kind of aeroplane
exercise: «The rain spoiled our picnic, but the hot chocolate was some compensation.» What is the hot chocolate? | A way to keep warm all day | A rainy day treat | A drink that the picnic shop sold | *Something that makes the bad picnic feel a little better
exercise: «She received ___ for her job, including wages and holidays.» Which word fits the gap? | A rainy day | A broken toy | A long walk | *Compensation
test: «The shop gave him a free game as compensation for the broken bike.» Why did the shop give him the game? | To say goodbye | To celebrate his birthday | *To make up for the broken bike | To sell him more games
test: Which phrase means given to make up for something that went wrong? | in a hurry | *as compensation | at the end of the day | for a laugh
exam: After the bus was cancelled, the company paid each passenger money in compensation. What does compensation mean? | A kind of seat | A type of bus ticket | *Money given to make up for the cancelled bus | Money paid for a holiday
